{
  "chapter": "evals/trajectory-evals",
  "tier": "drill",
  "notes": [
    "Scoring the path without specifying it. Six numbers, all in basis points, all rounded",
    "with floor(x + 0.5).",
    "Recall and precision are over the set of tools called, because which tools a ticket",
    "needs is a fact and the order it happened to visit them in is not.",
    "Order is scored only where the spec declares a policy pair. An effect that appears",
    "without its decision is a violation even when the decision arrives later, and even",
    "when the outcome was right.",
    "Step efficiency is the recorded minimum over the actual count, capped at 10000: a run",
    "that took fewer steps than the minimum skipped work, and recall is what catches that.",
    "Redundancy counts calls that contributed nothing. Loop escape counts only identical",
    "repeats of a call that already returned an error — a repeated success is waste, but a",
    "repeated failure is a control-flow signal."
  ],
  "cases": [
    {
      "id": "a-clean-run-scores-everything",
      "spec": { "required": ["get_order", "search_policies"], "minimumSteps": 2, "orderPolicy": [] },
      "calls": [
        { "tool": "get_order", "args": "4921", "error": null, "contributed": true },
        { "tool": "search_policies", "args": "RET-14", "error": null, "contributed": true }
      ],
      "result": {
        "recallBps": 10000,
        "precisionBps": 10000,
        "stepEfficiencyBps": 10000,
        "redundantBps": 0,
        "loopEscapeBps": 10000,
        "policyViolations": []
      }
    },
